ss><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAI ATSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, KEIJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAMITSU, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAI, ATSUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI KEIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURAMITSU HIDEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAI ATSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOBAYASHI, KEIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAMITSU, HIDEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAI, ATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A dielectric ceramic composition characterized by being formed by adding, to 100 moles of barium titanate with a Ba/Ti molar ratio of 1.001 to 1.05 as a main component, 0.5 to 5.0 moles of Mg in terms of MgO, 0.1 to 3.0 moles of Dy in terms of Dy2O3, 0.01 to 0.4 moles of Mn in terms of Mn3O4, 0.01 to 0.26 moles of V in terms of V2O5, 0.3 to 3.5 moles of Si in terms of SiO2 and 0.01 to 3.0 moles of Al in terms of Al2O3 as sub-components. The dielectric ceramic composition is used to produce a multilayer capacitor of which dielectric layer is not reduced even if an external electrode is formed by using a base metal such as copper and which has a high insulation resistance.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne une composition céramique diélectrique obtenue par adjonction, à 100 moles de titanate de baryum avec un rapport molaire de 1,001 à 1,05 comme composé principal, auxquels viennent s'ajouter  comme sous composants: de 0,5 à 5,0 moles de Mg sous forme de MgO, 0,1 à 3 moles de Dy sous forme de Dy2O3, 0,01 à 0,4 mole de Mn sous forme de Mn3O4, 0,01 à 0,26 mole de V sous forme de V2O5, 0,3 à 3,5 moles de Al sous forme de Al2O3. Cette composition céramique diélectrique sert à fabriquer un condensateur multicouche sur lequel la couche diélectrique n'est pas réduite même en cas de formation d'une électrode externe au moyen d'un métal de base telle que du cuivre, et qui présente une résistance élevée (isolation).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>